    "reference": "Authorization bead bu-nge1lu for implementation bead bu-4mfhdq (raw tool-call input is stripped to the capture allowlist before sessions.tool_calls is persisted; the spawner tool-call merge pairs a parser record that omits optional parameters with its executed wrapper capture by call order). Reviewed before: auth base d8d1f5c09cd94604e2feb4eb9b724fe75dd714c6 (main 7cbcbfa13 plus only the REQ-chronicler-api-017 ID header in openspec/specs/chronicler-api/spec.md) as recorded in bu-4mfhdq (sec-review-lane CORRECTIONS, then contract-review-lane recheck APPROVED CLEAN-pending-CE; the formal review bead opens with the DRAFT PR while the agent GitHub account is suspended); approved subject: agent/bu-4mfhdq head 2ce51cda33ae7b210c2903fa78dd9fa3248fb093, which tracks its request. Governing requirement REQ-chronicler-api-017. The 1 owner is the retained day-close writer case whose merged-record count moves from 2 to 1 because that merge now pairs the parser duplicate with its executed capture by call order when their input fingerprints differ. This exact manifest requires its own independent review and protected-main publication before consumption; provenance text grants no runtime admission."
  },
  "owners": [
    {
      "before": "tests/chronicler/test_day_close_writer.py::test_writer_accepts_executed_wrapper_capture_with_parser_duplicate_and_dst_window",
      "after": "tests/chronicler/test_day_close_writer.py::test_writer_accepts_executed_wrapper_capture_with_parser_duplicate_and_dst_window",
      "contracts": [
        "REQ-chronicler-api-017"
      ],
      "reason": "Only the merged-record count moves: the case builds a real Codex parser record for chronicler_day_close_bundle that omits the handler defaults and a real executed capture from the wrapper, and previously asserted len(merged_calls) == 2 because the fingerprints differed and the parser duplicate stayed unpaired. The merge now pairs them, so the count is 1 (REQ-chronicler-api-017 scenario 'A parser call that omits optional parameters pairs with its executed capture'). The assertion that exactly one record carries an outcome, the writer's acceptance of the merged list (invalid_reason None, two execute calls, the upserted date_label and DST-window start/end) and the case id are unchanged; the single record keeps the canonical chronicler_day_close_bundle name the writer validates."
    }
